    "stem": "Prove D_KL(P‖Q)≥0 using Jensen's inequality.",
    "rubric": {
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "element-1",
          "description": "D_KL(P‖Q) = E_P[−log(Q(X)/P(X))]",
          "weight": 1,
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "id": "element-2",
          "description": "since −log is convex, Jensen gives E_P[−log(Q(X)/P(X))] ≥ −log(E_P[Q(X)/P(X)])",
          "weight": 1,
          "required": false
        },
        {
          "id": "element-3",
          "description": "E_P[Q(X)/P(X)] = Σₓ P(x)·Q(x)/P(x) = Σₓ Q(x) = 1 over P's support, so the bound is −log(1)=0  — a direct reuse of `jensen-inequality`",
          "weight": 1,
          "required": false
        }
      ]
    },
